\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. O Lord of every lovely thing,
\par The Maker of them all,
\par Who from the winter's gloomy wing
\par Dost shed the splendours of the spring,
\par On Thy great name we call.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. With flowers that through the valleys teach
\par Thy love and truth divine,
\par With streams that sing, and hills that preach,
\par With waves that laugh on every beach,
\par We praise Thee we are Thine!\tab 
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Not Thine alone because from Thee
\par Our life and breath we hold;
\par But Thine because in Christ we see
\par The grace that sets our spirits free,
\par And for the truth makes bold.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Count as amongst the radiant choir
\par That sounds Thy name abroad,
\par Set in our lands the heavenly lyre,
\par With songs of love our hearts inspire,
\par The mighty love of God.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Until with those who toiled and dreamed
\par To build Thy kingdom here,
\par With those the world hath ne'er esteemed,
\par With all the hosts of Thy redeemed,
\par We in Thy home appear.
\par 
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

